From: RE-CS-06 minimal build
Subject: [PATCH] net: preserve allocated dummy NAPI netdev state

Fix the common allocator, used by PPE Direct Switch and ath12k NAPI.
Keep init_dummy_netdev() behavior for embedded dummy devices unchanged.

diff --git a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.18/0677-net-preserve-allocated-dummy-netdev-state.patch b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.18/0677-net-preserve-allocated-dummy-netdev-state.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.18/0677-net-preserve-allocated-dummy-netdev-state.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+From: RE-CS-06 minimal build
+Subject: [PATCH] net: do not clear allocated resources in dummy netdev setup
+
+alloc_netdev() allocates the address list and reference tracking before
+invoking its setup callback. init_dummy_netdev() clears the entire object,
+losing those allocations and leaving dev_addr NULL. free_netdev() then
+crashes in dev_addr_check(). Use a non-destructive callback for allocated
+dummy devices, retaining the existing initialization for embedded devices.
+This affects both PPE Direct Switch and ath12k NAPI netdev teardown.
+The destructive setup was restored by generic/hack-6.18/991-revert-
+init_dummy_netdev.patch without splitting the allocated-device callback.
+
+--- a/net/core/dev.c
++++ b/net/core/dev.c
+@@ -12323,6 +12323,14 @@ void free_netdev(struct net_device *dev)
+ }
+ EXPORT_SYMBOL(free_netdev);
+ 
++static void setup_allocated_dummy_netdev(struct net_device *dev)
++{
++	/* alloc_netdev() has already initialized the core allocation state. */
++	dev->reg_state = NETREG_DUMMY;
++	set_bit(__LINK_STATE_PRESENT, &dev->state);
++	set_bit(__LINK_STATE_START, &dev->state);
++}
++
+ /**
+  * alloc_netdev_dummy - Allocate and initialize a dummy net device.
+  * @sizeof_priv: size of private data to allocate space for
+@@ -12332,6 +12340,6 @@ struct net_device *alloc_netdev_dummy(int sizeof_priv)
+ {
+ 	return alloc_netdev(sizeof_priv, "dummy#", NET_NAME_UNKNOWN,
+-			    init_dummy_netdev);
++			    setup_allocated_dummy_netdev);
+ }
+ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(alloc_netdev_dummy);
+ 
